&lt;p&gt;Qube Research &amp;amp; Technologies (QRT) is a global quantitative and systematic investment manager, operating in all liquid asset classes across the world. We are a technology and data driven group implementing a scientific approach to investing. Combining data, research, technology, and trading expertise has shaped QRT’s collaborative mindset which enables us to solve the most complex challenges. QRT’s culture of innovation continuously drives our ambition to deliver high quality returns for our investors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;&quot; data-start=&quot;166&quot; data-end=&quot;512&quot;&gt;We’re looking for an experienced recruiter to join our Talent Acquisition team and help drive hiring for quantitative research and trading roles across Europe. This role plays a key part in supporting QRT’s continued growth by securing top-tier talent and reinforcing our local presence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Future Role at QRT&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Drive and execute QRT’s recruitment strategy to attract, hire, and retain high calibre quant research and trading talent for our European offices&lt;br&gt;• Leverage your existing network across Europe and proactively source candidates through direct outreach, talent mapping, and referrals&lt;br&gt;• Collaborate with trusted external recruitment partners and agencies to ensure consistent pipeline flow and meet headcount targets&lt;br&gt;• Own and manage the full recruitment lifecycle via our ATS (Greenhouse), ensuring a high-touch, seamless candidate experience at every stage&lt;br&gt;• Bring hiring intelligence and market insights to the table - tracking trends, benchmarking competitors, and advising stakeholders&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your present skillset&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• 5+ years of experience recruiting in quantitative finance, trading, or investment roles – either in-house or at a leading search firm&lt;br&gt;• A strong, active network of talent across Europe, and a proven ability to build and sustain candidate relationships over time&lt;br&gt;• Track record of successful collaboration with external agencies&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• Proficiency with recruiting tools and platforms, especially Greenhouse and LinkedIn&lt;br&gt;• Data-driven mindset, you use metrics, hiring funnel data, and market benchmarks to inform decisions&lt;br&gt;• Excellent written and verbal communication skills in English&lt;br&gt;• Organized, resourceful, you are able to juggle multiple searches with speed and precision&lt;br&gt;• Self-starter and curious, you like working in a fast-paced, high-performance environment&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;QRT is an equal opportunity employer. We welcome diversity as essential to our success. QRT empowers employees to work openly and respectfully to achieve collective success. In addition to professional achievement, we are offering initiatives and programs to enable employees achieve a healthy work-life balance.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Protect and build a future shaped by original ideas, innovations, and creativity.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Threats to brand integrity are scaling fast. We&#39;re building the intelligence to scale faster. MarqVision is the brand integrity partner for the world&#39;s most ambitious companies, providing AI-powered enforcement and intelligence across 1,500+ platforms in 115+ countries. We don&#39;t just flag problems; we eliminate them at scale so brands can grow with confidence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2020 by Harvard Law graduates and backed by leading investors including SoftBank, Y Combinator, DST Global Partners, HSG, and Salesforce Ventures, we&#39;ve built the category-defining platform for brand protection. We&#39;re recognized with an LVMH Innovation Award and named to the Inc. 5000 Fastest Growing Companies in 2025, and we&#39;re just getting started.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you want to work at the intersection of AI, global commerce, and IP, this is the place. We&#39;re pushing the boundaries of brand control to keep innovation, creativity, and trust safeguarded in a rapidly evolving digital world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How You&#39;ll Make an Impact at MarqVision&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Account Executive focused on EMEA, you&#39;ll own the full sales cycle and help protect the world&#39;s most recognizable brands, from global luxury houses to emerging streetwear labels and leading names in health, wellness, and beauty, against the growing threat of IP infringement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partnering closely with Sales Leadership in North America and APAC, you will help brand partners identify and act against bad actors responsible for millions in lost revenue, fraudulent sales, and long-term brand damage each year. Your work will sit at the intersection of cutting-edge technology and real-world brand protection, giving you the opportunity to drive meaningful commercial impact for clients who are serious about safeguarding what they&#39;ve built.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consult prospective clients on tailored brand protection strategies and how MarqVision&#39;s platform addresses their specific challenges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver compelling product demonstrations that bring to life the platform&#39;s ability to detect, enforce against, and eliminate counterfeit activity at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead high-quality discovery calls, business reviews, and demo sessions with potential customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own pipeline progression and closing new business against quarterly revenue targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Sales Development Representatives to execute strategic outbound campaigns&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills You Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of closing experience in a B2B SaaS sales role, with a consistent track record of meeting or exceeding quarterly revenue targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to manage complex, consultative sales cycles of 3–6 months and close deals with ACVs in the £37,000–£112,000 range&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confident and proactive pipeline building, comfort self-sourcing opportunities alongside SDR support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience engaging and influencing senior executives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Signal&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in Spanish or German&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of closing enterprise-level accounts&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sector experience in fashion, cosmetics, or other consumer products&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with intellectual property, brand protection, or anti-counterfeiting, whether through prior roles or genuine personal interest&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical application of structured sales methodologies (i.e. MEDDPIC)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Become a Marqvisioner&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous PTO to take the time you need, when you need it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid work model designed for focus and flexibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equity in every offer — because you should own a piece of what you&#39;re building&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive health, dental, and vision coverage, plus parental leave to support your life outside of work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pension plan to help you save for the future&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A one-time home office stipend for remote employees — because your setup should work as hard as you do&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Protect what&#39;s original. Scale what&#39;s possible. At MarqVision, we believe real growth comes with attracting the brightest minds, motivating them to succeed in their position, and ensuring plenty of fun along the way. If you think this position is for you, apply now.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;MarqVision is an Equal Opportunity Employer and encourages applicants of all backgrounds to apply. We are committed to building a diverse and inclusive workforce that reflects the customers and communities we serve. Your privacy is important to us. By applying for this role, you acknowledge MarqVision’s Global Recruiting Privacy Policy. Please review our &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rWdOaSaiZyfYVVP71sQfPd-XnV93oVmFyjP8URCnHJg/edit?tab=t.0&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt; for details.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role OVO-View&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Hybrid – Hub-based (Bristol, Glasgow, or London) + Work from Home&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contract &amp;amp; Salary:&lt;/strong&gt; 12-Month FTC | £45,000 – £51,665 + Up to 15% Discretionary Bonus + 9% Flex Pay&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3-Word Snapshot:&lt;/strong&gt; Detail | Regulation | Impact&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Visa Sponsorship:&lt;/strong&gt; Unfortunately, we are unable to offer sponsorship for this role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why this role matters:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At OVO, our mission is simple but huge: solve the climate crisis through &lt;strong&gt;Plan Zero&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Compliance Analyst&lt;/strong&gt; in our &lt;strong&gt;Policy &amp;amp; Regulation&lt;/strong&gt; team, you&#39;ll be instrumental in steering our strategic compliance initiatives and maintaining regulatory excellence. By translating complex energy regulations into practical operational advice, you will help bake risk mitigation directly into our long-term business decisions as we drive toward net zero.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll be doing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting directly to the &lt;strong&gt;Senior Compliance Manager&lt;/strong&gt;, you&#39;ll work independently to keep our regulatory compliance activities running seamlessly:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Regulatory Advice:&lt;/strong&gt; Dissect complex regulations and translate them into clear guidance for commercial and operational leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Evidence-Backed Risk Assessments:&lt;/strong&gt; Conduct deep-dive research across OVO and the external landscape to deliver well-evidenced risk assessments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clear &amp;amp; Influential Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; Draft polished briefings, advice, and reports ready for senior leadership and regulatory audiences like Ofgem with minimal rework.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regulatory Preparedness:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead the groundwork and evidence-gathering for regulatory submissions and major compliance projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance Culture Advocacy:&lt;/strong&gt; Champion regulatory integrity and the Standards of Conduct across OVO, helping teams flag risks early.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll bring to the table:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You don’t need to tick every single box to apply - if you have the core toolkit and a passion for problem-solving, we want to hear from you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Essentials:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Energy Regulation Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Direct experience reading and translating complex energy regulations into clear guidance for non-specialist operational teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regulatory Engagement:&lt;/strong&gt; Confidence engaging with external stakeholders, including energy regulator Ofgem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analytical Precision &amp;amp; Curiosity:&lt;/strong&gt; A keen eye for detail, pride in accuracy, and a natural curiosity to ask better questions and spot risks early.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Autonomy &amp;amp; Organisation:&lt;/strong&gt; Ability to manage your own time, prioritise multiple workstreams, and meet deadlines without needing to be prompted.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborative Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong written and verbal skills, with a track record of building trusted working relationships across a business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have (but not essential):&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience using workflow tools like &lt;strong&gt;Jira&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Where &amp;amp; how you’ll work:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe in flexibility that works. You’ll be assigned to your closest hub office (&lt;strong&gt;Bristol, Glasgow, or London&lt;/strong&gt;). We expect hub-based team members in the office at least once a week for collaborative days and in-person OVO Connection events, combined with flexible work-from-home options.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What’s in it for you?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We reward impact. On top of your core salary (&lt;strong&gt;£45,000–£51,665&lt;/strong&gt; depending on experience), you’ll get:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;15% On-Target Bonus:&lt;/strong&gt; Discretionary, tied to our collective Plan Zero mission performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;9% Flex Pay:&lt;/strong&gt; An extra 9% on top of your salary (4% auto-enrolled into pension, 5% yours to take as cash, put into pension, or spend on flex benefits).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Time Off:&lt;/strong&gt; 34 days of holiday (including bank holidays).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Green &amp;amp; Home Perks:&lt;/strong&gt; Up to £400 towards OVO Energy plans, plus discounts on solar, smart thermostats, and EV chargers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Health &amp;amp; Lifestyle:&lt;/strong&gt; Healthcare cash plan / private medical options, gym discounts, cycle-to-work scheme, and ultra-low emission car leasing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Everyone Belongs at OVO:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Changing the world takes all of us. We are committed to building a diverse and inclusive workplace representing all gender identities, ethnicities, abilities, ages, and backgrounds. We also have &lt;strong&gt;8 employee-led Belonging Networks&lt;/strong&gt; you can join from day one.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Need accommodations during the application process? Let us know on your application form - we’re here to make the process as easy and comfortable for you as possible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ready to make a difference?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If this sounds like your next challenge, hit &lt;strong&gt;Apply Now&lt;/strong&gt; - even if you don&#39;t feel you hit 100% of the criteria!&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;💼 About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Cryptography Software Engineer to join our team to help design and implement the next generation of secure Embedded Software implementations of Classic &amp;amp; Post Quantum Cryptography.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have been established since 2018, so you would be directly working with the founders and inventors of this deep tech startup. The technology is already a couple of years in the making, its feasibility having been established, funding secured, and it has a clear path to market. This is a great opportunity&amp;nbsp; for career progression and to get a head start in a rapidly expanding segment of the semiconductor industry (Post-Quantum Cryptography and RISC-V).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our platform IP components come together as a RISC-V MCU based Sub-system with advanced (post-quantum) cryptography algorithm support and security features.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Software Engineer at PQShield, you will be designing and developing secure solutions, helping to develop software solutions working seamlessly through the entire software development life cycle. You will assist with the development of PQShield&#39;s core software cryptography libraries.&amp;nbsp; Responsibilities include developing internal tools to support the build, test and security analysis of PQShield&#39;s software products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;⚒️ What you’ll be doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, implement, and test classical and post-quantum cryptographic primitives with a strong emphasis on functional correctness, interoperability, and optimized performance across software environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and integrate cryptographic solutions on hardware platforms, including FPGA and hardware cryptographic coprocessors, with a focus on acceleration and secure implementation on ARM and RISC-V architectures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Harden cryptographic implementations against side-channel analysis (SCA), fault injection attacks (FIA), and other physical or logical threats through constant-time design and other countermeasures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensuring integration with cryptographic system and application API’s, for example: GlobalPlatform, ARM Platform Security Architecture, Linux Kernel drivers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with cryptographers, security engineers, and cross-functional teams—including hardware, verification, and platform security—to review, validate, and harden cryptographic implementations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to performance benchmarking and optimization across multiple platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to design and code review meetings to improve cryptographic software quality, architecture, and development processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform and support security-focused code reviews, including static and dynamic analysis, and apply formal methods such as model checking where applicable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and enhance existing cryptographic software, ensuring robustness, security, and performance across supported platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support compliance with relevant security standards (e.g., FIPS, ISO/IEC, NIST PQC).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in threat modeling and risk assessments related to cryptographic software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🎯 Required Skills And Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master’s or PhD degree in computer science, mathematics, or a related field, with a strong background in cryptography or computer security.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in C and Assembly, with a focus on resource-constrained, bare-metal environments. Experience with Rust is nice to have.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with classical and post-quantum cryptographic algorithms, including NIST PQC candidates, and a solid understanding of NIST and FIPS publications and compliance requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent problem-solving and debugging skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;👍 Preferred Skills And Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with secure coding practices and countermeasures against implementation attacks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of side-channel attacks (timing, power, EM), fault attacks, and corresponding mitigation strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with or working knowledge of security certification frameworks such as FIPS 140-3, SESIP, PSA Certified, or Common Criteria.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read and implement specifications from cryptographic research papers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of professional experience in cryptographic software engineering is preferred; however, we assess seniority primarily based on your depth of knowledge, hands-on experience, and problem-solving skills rather than just years worked.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🏆 Some of the perks of working with us:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unparalleled opportunities to learn and accelerated career development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative, team environment with people who truly love what they do.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary and share option scheme.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;hybrid&amp;nbsp;working, and a working from home budget.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Private health insurance for yourself and your family.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 days annual leave (plus bank holidays and two wellness weeks).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;50% gym membership discount.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The chance to work with a spirited, smart, and friendly team!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;PQShield is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. We’re passionate about talent and proud to foster an inclusive environment; all applicants will be considered regardless of their gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability, and age.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p data-local-id=&quot;c72cb78accbb&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;paragraph&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot; data-pm-slice=&quot;1 3 []&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;mark&quot; data-prosemirror-mark-name=&quot;strong&quot;&gt;Lead Software Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-local-id=&quot;9203abde8e4c&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;paragraph&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;mark&quot; data-prosemirror-mark-name=&quot;strong&quot;&gt;Reports to: Director of Engineering&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-local-id=&quot;00cf1dcafad5&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;paragraph&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;mark&quot; data-prosemirror-mark-name=&quot;strong&quot;&gt;Department: Engineering&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-local-id=&quot;3eb2b3cabd8f&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;paragraph&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-local-id=&quot;fac87f3088b1&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;paragraph&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;mark&quot; data-prosemirror-mark-name=&quot;strong&quot;&gt;💼 About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-local-id=&quot;d2fcf4f24bf0&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;paragraph&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot;&gt;PQShield is looking for a Lead Software Engineer to help lead a cryptographic software IP team. As a Lead Software Engineer, you will be responsible for overseeing the entire software development lifecycle, from design to testing, and ensuring the delivery of high-quality software solutions. This includes planning, organizing, and managing the software development, including setting timelines, allocating resources, and tracking progress. You will work across a variety of environments, solving complex problems and developing other engineers, while maintaining a strong focus on quality and best practices. You will support the hiring, training, and managing of a team of software engineers, fostering collaboration, and resolving conflicts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-local-id=&quot;2f02d251f599&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;paragraph&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;ddad4c96-18bd-4352-be80-d6bb3e55ea2e&quot; data-mark-type=&quot;annotation&quot; data-mark-annotation-type=&quot;inlineComment&quot; data-id=&quot;ddad4c96-18bd-4352-be80-d6bb3e55ea2e&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;mark&quot; data-prosemirror-mark-name=&quot;annotation&quot;&gt;Candidates should hold a degree in Electronic Engineering/Computer Science or equivalent experience, backed by at least 10 years in software design and/or verification. We are looking for a technical lead—or a senior engineer ready to step up into leadership—to guide our team. Knowledge of cryptographic engineering and side-channel attack resistance is a major bonus. You should be ready to contribute to cross-team strategy, lead architectural reviews, and drive planning for your team.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-local-id=&quot;e1253695958c&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;paragraph&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;20e0d5a7-c8b2-476c-8a72-8438da12e0ce&quot; data-mark-type=&quot;annotation&quot; data-mark-annotation-type=&quot;inlineComment&quot; data-id=&quot;20e0d5a7-c8b2-476c-8a72-8438da12e0ce&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;mark&quot; data-prosemirror-mark-name=&quot;annotation&quot;&gt;Founded in 2018, we are a well-funded deep tech startup with proven technology and a clear path to market. Joining us now offers a unique opportunity to work directly with our founders and inventors, fast-track your career progression, and shape a rapidly expanding segment of the semiconductor industry (Post-Quantum Cryptography and RISC-V).&lt;/span&gt; This is a great opportunity&amp;nbsp; for career progression and to get a head start in a rapidly expanding segment of the semiconductor industry (Post-Quantum Cryptography and RISC-V).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-local-id=&quot;df4c222c6338&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;paragraph&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-local-id=&quot;24490093d3f7&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;paragraph&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;mark&quot; data-prosemirror-mark-name=&quot;strong&quot;&gt;⚒️ What you’ll be doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-local-id=&quot;4051e37fd161&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;paragraph&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Working with other &lt;span id=&quot;43aa3e8e-802b-4816-a127-8abfa7ee5606&quot; data-mark-type=&quot;annotation&quot; data-mark-annotation-type=&quot;inlineComment&quot; data-id=&quot;43aa3e8e-802b-4816-a127-8abfa7ee5606&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;mark&quot; data-prosemirror-mark-name=&quot;annotation&quot;&gt;engineering leaders&lt;/span&gt; and project managers to plan and allocate work, ensuring we are delivering on our product roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
